{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781363912,"nonce":"4pXPSINKlvbhBc2xBD6n37ozwMg=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFYRRTQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/259","origin":"github"},"title":"Add screenshooter crop+timestamp utility (crop_screenshooter.sh)","message":"## Summary\n\nAdd `bizzyboat_project11/scripts/crop_screenshooter.sh`: a utility to crop an\noperator **screenshooter** time-lapse to the useful region(s) and burn the real\nper-frame wall-clock timestamp onto each frame, so frames can be traced back to\nbag data during debriefs.\n\n## Why\n\nThe screenshooter (`ccomjhc_project11/scripts/screenshooter.bash`) records the\nfull 3840x5760 3-monitor operator screen at 2 fps. For review we usually want a\nsingle screen band (CAMP/chart + camera grid + segmentation + sidescan), not the\nwhole stack, and we need a real timestamp on each frame to jump back into the\nbags. The screenshooter already writes a sidecar `operator_\u003cdate\u003e.csv`\n(`frame_index,timestamp(UTC),filename`), so the per-frame time is recoverable\nexactly (capture interval is variable ~30-44 s, so an assumed interval is wrong).\n\n## What\n\n- Region presets (tuned to the current operator monitor layout):\n  - `middle` (default) — annunciator + CAMP/chart + camera grid + segmentation +\n    bottom sidescan waterfall. `crop=3840:2250:0:2000`.\n  - `top-middle` — the above plus the top screen. `crop=3840:4250:0:0`.\n  - raw `w:h:x:y` override also accepted.\n- Burns `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS UTC (HH:MM:SS EDT)` per frame from the CSV (UTC\n  matches ROS message epoch; EDT matches local-time bag dir names). Timestamp\n  bottom-left so it does not cover the annunciator panel.\n- Output to `~/data/logs/analysis/\u003cdate\u003e_screenshooter_crop/`.\n\nCrop geometry is layout-specific and documented in the script header for\nre-tuning if the operator monitor arrangement changes.\n\nSurfaced during the 2026-06-12 Lake Massabesic shakedown debrief.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}